<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 30 August, from 1363 to 1999.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1363 <span class="tih-ago">663 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Lake Poyang begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The fleets of Zhu Yuanzhang and Chen Youliang clashed on Lake Poyang in one of the largest naval battles in history. Zhu's victory weeks later opened his path to founding the Ming dynasty.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/australia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/australia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1835 <span class="tih-ago">191 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Pascoe Fawkner's settlers land at the site of Melbourne</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Settlers sent by John Pascoe Fawkner went ashore on the Yarra River, building the first houses of what became Melbourne. It grew into Australia's second-largest city.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1905 <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ty Cobb makes his major league debut</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Eighteen-year-old Ty Cobb hit a double in his first game for the Detroit Tigers. His lifetime batting average of .366 remains the highest in major league history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/moscow" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moscow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1963 <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Washington-Moscow hotline goes into service</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A direct teleprinter link between the White House and the Kremlin began operating. Set up after the Cuban missile crisis, it aimed to prevent war by misunderstanding; it was never a red telephone.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/east-timor" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/east-timor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1999 <span class="tih-ago">27 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">East Timor votes for independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a UN-run referendum, 78.5 per cent of East Timorese voted for independence from Indonesia. Militia violence followed until an Australian-led force restored order; independence came in 2002.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-timor">East Timor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a></div></div></li></ol>
